ute. Its labels disagree: Plans / Billing / Subscription / `PricingPage`. |\n| `src/date.ts` | Same directory, with its own date problems. Worth checking before adding any time logic. |\n\n## Risks the scan flagged in `billing.ts`\n\n**High**\n1. **`Invoice` contract split (crime_00026):** `src/api/state.ts`'s `Invoice` has 2 fields; this file's has 11. It lacks `createdAt`, `currency`, `discountCents`, `subtotalCents`, `taxCents` and `userId`, and nothing checks the two against each other.\n2. **`User` contract split (crime_00010):** the `src/api/state.ts` version lacks `createdAt`.\n3. **`generateInvoice` is too long (crime_00033):** 204 lines, 3.4× the 60-line threshold. A change in one section can easily affect another.\n\n**Medium**\n4. **Misleading name (crime_00012):** `calculateRefundPreview` sounds pure but has side effects (an audit write and an email).\n5. **Rule only in a comment (crime_00013):** the L39 refund rule for owners and enterprise plans isn't encoded anywhere.\n6. **Commented-out code (crime_00028):** the dead `legacyRefund` block at L33–37.\n7. **Direct clock reads (crime_00029):** 7 uses of `Date.now()` / `new Date()` (L57, 63, 92, 198, 238, 250, 273). None of them decide a branch, but the output can't be tested without a fixed clock.\n8. **Scattered `\"enterprise\"` literal (crime_00004):** it appears in 4 files.\n9. **File too large (crime_00036):** 310 lines.\n\n**Low**\n10. **Swallowed error (crime_00032):** in `generateInvoice` (L245–247), the catch block holds only an `XXX` comment, so callers can't tell the email failed.\n11. **Unresolved markers (crime_00039):** 4 TODO/FIXME/HACK/XXX comments between L183 and L308.\n\n**In the neighbouring test file:** `src/billing.test.ts` has a test with no assertions (\"renders the enterprise plan\") and one with only a weak matcher (\"creates an invoice\"). It also imports `vitest`, which isn't declared in `package.json`. Passing tests won't prove much.\n\n**Scan warnings:** one suppression entry